<control>{"schema":"stage-control-v1","digest":"The prefix fallback demonstrably accepts unrelated Errors; downstream diagnostic suppression remains unverified.","findingId":"finding-006","finding":"Stop-error matching accepts unrelated failures with a similar message prefix","verdict":"KEEP","evidence":[{"file":"src/workflow-stop.ts","line":55,"lineEnd":57,"symbol":"isWorkflowStopRequestedError","quote":"error instanceof Error &&\n\t\t(error.name === WORKFLOW_STOP_REQUESTED_ERROR_NAME ||\n\t\t\terror.message.startsWith(\"workflow stop requested\"))"},{"file":"src/workflow-stop.ts","line":44,"symbol":"workflowStopRequestedMessage","quote":"return `workflow stop requested for ${runId}`;"},{"file":"src/workflow-stop.ts","line":49,"symbol":"createWorkflowStopRequestedError","quote":"error.name = WORKFLOW_STOP_REQUESTED_ERROR_NAME;"},{"file":"src/workflow-stop.ts","line":35,"symbol":"createWorkflowStopPendingError","quote":"error.name = WORKFLOW_STOP_PENDING_ERROR_NAME;"}],"counterEvidence":["The instanceof Error guard excludes plain strings and plain records; the false-positive scope is limited to Error instances.","Canonical stop errors already receive the dedicated WorkflowStopRequested name, so their classification is intentional."],"recommendedAction":"Prefer the explicit stop sentinel. If legacy message-only errors must remain supported, compare against the exact expected-run message without overriding conflicting error names. Add regression tests for similarly prefixed operational failures and WorkflowStopPending errors."}</control>

<analysis>The finding survives attempted refutation. For new Error("workflow stop requested but persistence failed: EACCES"), instanceof Error is true, the dedicated-name comparison is false, and startsWith is true. The classifier therefore returns true despite the message not matching the generated stop-message format.

The fallback also overrides conflicting classifications: an error created by createWorkflowStopPendingError with that message is recognized as stop-requested despite its distinct WorkflowStopPending name. The named-error branch does not protect against this because the branches are joined by OR.

This establishes the classifier defect, not an observed operational incident. The supplied repository is an excerpt without consumers or the imported store implementation; diagnostic suppression and production reachability remain applicability caveats, not counter-evidence against the demonstrated behavior.

